": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e2be7bae89871b42d54400d5ae0bfd0429f8a7d154360dceb6457b22d6b4d00a","event_uuid":"a65e1a4d-d456-4684-8a45-4bf1d0b8e512","position":{"commit_sha":"d8636c559b8669e46b0957262a6fb674b57b043e","position":"1788473548549867267-a65e1a4d-d456-4684-8a45-4bf1d0b8e512"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Claimed; beginning held-out TDD in worktree janitor-38ab-928f.","timestamp":1788468880065392001},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementer update: added conflict-safe sidecar transaction seam and migrated peer confirmations, impossible links, mapping/provenance, HLC, and recent-creates to shared sibling locks where applicable. Verified in /Users/joeoakhart/janitor-38ab-928f with targeted pytest (53 passed), make typecheck (success), and make lint (success).","timestamp":1788469509837130347},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented conflict-safe reconciler sidecar persistence in worktree janitor-38ab-928f. RED held-out oracle exposed distinct-key clobber and delete resurrection. GREEN held-out oracle passed. Sandbox mutation check reintroduced snapshot overwrite and oracle failed as expected. Targeted impacted tests passed (53 passed); lint and typecheck passed. Full make test was attempted and stopped on pre-existing/unrelated tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py failure.","timestamp":1788472820465224001}],"created_at":1788313621839043001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a65e1a4d-d456-4684-8a45-4bf1d0b8e512","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"44f8-01c7-6f14-419f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe current tests inspect replacement mechanics or final JSON rather than the write window (`test_applier_mapping.py:235-282`, `test_applier_provenance.py:155-185`), permit last-writer record loss (`test_bridge_state_atomic_write_concurrency.py:41-120`), and source-grep impossible-link durability (`test_impossible_links_cicada.py:467-493`). Live sidecars replace full snapshots in `peer_confirmations.py:192-217` and `impossible_links.py:376-401`. The repository already has sibling-file locked read-modify-write prior art in `_store/hlc.py::_hlc_lock` and `_commands/recent_creates.py::_journal_lock`, plus durable same-directory publication in `_store/fsutil.py::atomic_write`.\n\n## Approach\n\nGeneralize the established sibling-lock pattern in `rebar._store.fsutil` as a narrow reusable exclusive-path-lock context manager. Migrate HLC and recent-create callers to it so the project has one standard lock implementation. A lock lives at a stable sibling `.lock` path, never on the replaceable JSON inode, and remains an untracked local control artifact for the lifetime of its sidecar workspace; commit-back must not stage it. The context spans re-read, mutation, `fsutil.atomic_write(fsync=True)`, and unlock.\n\nAdd `sidecar_transactions.py` only for the reconciler-specific part that existing prior art does not provide: applying a domain mutation or record delta while the shared `fsutil` lock is held. It delegates all locking and atomic publication to the generalized `fsutil` seams. Mapping/provenance mutations load the current valid mapping under that lock, apply their key-level mutation, then publish it.\n\nFor peer-confirmation and impossible-link stores, take an independent deep copy of the records loaded at construction as the immutable baseline. At save, calculate upserts and deletions against that copy; while holding the shared lock, reload the latest valid record set and apply the delta. Different keys survive. The concrete same-key rule is last shared-lock holder wins, including a deletion, so the test can assert the later lock acquisition order.\n\nIf loading valid JSON, acquiring the lock, or publishing fails, preserve the target bytes, log a path-specific warning, skip persistence for that pass, and continue the reconciliation pass fail-open. This includes malformed/non-object JSON. Readers retain old-or-new complete-document visibility through `fsutil.atomic_write(fsync=True)`. Fresh-reader tests prove the existing commit-back path publishes valid state.\n\n## Scope\n\n- generalized sibling locking and durable publication reuse in `src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py`\n- HLC and recent-create adoption of that single lock seam\n- reconciler-specific `sidecar_transactions.py` delta application; mapping, peer-confirmation, and impossible-link callers\n- focused concurrency, mapping, provenance, malformed-state, and durability tests\n\n## Testing\n\nCharacterize HLC and recent-create lock migration against the prior behavior. Use barrier-controlled independent writers, same-key writers, a delete-versus-write pair, and an in-window reader for sidecars. Verify a deep baseline detects both in-place upserts and deletes, verify every lock/load/publish failure warns without overwriting, verify `.lock` files are not commit-back inputs, and prove durability through a fresh reader.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `fsutil` exposes the one sibling-path exclusive-lock primitive used by HLC, recent-create, and reconciler sidecar transactions; each caller holds it over its complete read-modify-write window.\n- [ ] The stable `.lock` file is never staged or published by commit-back and is intentionally retained for reuse while its sidecar workspace exists.\n- [ ] Reconciler sidecar publication delegates to `fsutil.atomic_write(fsync=True)` rather than reimplementing temp-file replacement.\n- [ ] Mapping/provenance updates load the latest valid mapping under the shared lock before applying their key-level mutation.\n- [ ] Peer-confirmation and impossible-link stores calculate their upserts and deletions from an independent deep copy of the load-time records.\n- [ ] Concurrent distinct-key updates retain both records; a same-key test proves the later shared-lock holder wins.\n- [ ] A delete-versus-write test proves a deliberate impossible-link deletion is propagated and a later shared-lock holder determines the same-key outcome.\n- [ ] An in-window reader sees only complete pre- or post-transaction JSON.\n- [ ] A malformed target, lock failure, or atomic-write failure logs the sidecar path, preserves its bytes, and allows the reconciliation pass to continue.\n- [ ] A fresh reader proves committed mapping and impossible-link state survives publication.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py","reason":"generalize established sibling-path exclusive locking and retain fsyncing atomic publication"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/hlc.py","reason":"migrate existing HLC lock ownership to the generalized fsutil seam"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/recent_creates.py","reason":"migrate established journal lock to the generalized fsutil seam"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/sidecar_transactions.py","reason":"new reconciler-specific delta application that composes shared lock and publication seams"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/pass_io.py","reason":"route mapping and provenance mutations through the shared transaction"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/peer_confirmations.py","reason":"keep independent baseline snapshots and delegate delta persistence"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/impossible_links.py","reason":"keep independent baseline snapshots and delegate delete-aware persistence"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_mapping.py","reason":"observe locked mapping and provenance updates"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_applier_provenance.py","reason":"observe atomic provenance behavior"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_bridge_state_atomic_write_concurrency.py","reason":"prove shared-lock merge, LWW, deletion, reader visibility, and failure disposition"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_impossible_links_cicada.py","reason":"prove durable commit-back through a fresh reader"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_hlc.py","reason":"characterize HLC behavior across generalized lock migration"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86"],["relates_to","44f8-01c7-6f14-419f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","parent_status_uuid":"90f426a8-8d08-45ed-8e86-b07c1122d8ae","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","reconciler","concurrency","rp16"],"ticket_id":"38ab-928f-edf3-4d0b","ticket_type":"story","title":"Make reconciliation sidecar persistence conflict-safe and observationally proven","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["824403d6-ffa2-41c3-9cdb-7113c8831bef","3f8abbde-19e7-412b-95cb-db380c2e68d7","bb1ef976-e50b-4b5b-8f96-ece881ce5b5c","5514769b-ae04-41d0-a507-ae0b6d3de23a","b5bef070-df3f-4a48-97ab-a5d52f59b042","9e385f1e-9a82-4b3c-a830-4bab69014e5e","90f426a8-8d08-45ed-8e86-b07c1122d8ae","53e5b34b-7baf-4ec7-9084-22308d0577bb","ec32edfe-d8e6-4452-93bb-49ccbdd84ca5","afa1ec12-e4af-4f14-9a76-9d2935de7f4c","f5967719-d0c5-4f29-981c-f2b3f8f6d151","a65e1a4d-d456-4684-8a45-4bf1d0b8e512"]},"env_id":"b8a